# Project Layout — Three Pillars

Exactly three source projects. Respect boundaries; do not blur them.

| Project | Role | Ships? |
|---------|------|--------|
| `POE2Radar.Core` | Memory plumbing, `Poe2Offsets`, `Poe2Live`, pathfinding math | DLL dep |
| `POE2Radar.Overlay` | Tick loop, ImGui overlay, HTTP API, config, input | **The `.exe`** |
| `POE2Radar.Research` | Offset discovery, probes, DevTree | Dev-only |

## Dependency rules

- **Overlay → Core** only. **Research → Core** only.
- **Never** reference Overlay or Research from Core.
- **Never** link Research into Overlay (no `ProjectReference`, no shared copy-paste of probe code into overlay).
- Tests: `POE2Radar.Core.Tests` → Core; `POE2Radar.Overlay.Tests` → Overlay.

## Where code belongs

| Concern | Location |
|---------|----------|
| `ReadProcessMemory`, structs, offsets, live reads | `Core/Game/`, `Core/Pathfinding/` |
| Drawing, ImGui, hotkeys, settings JSON, dashboard | `Overlay/` |
| AOB scan, `--hp`, `--devtree`, atlas probes | `Research/` |

## Platform

- `net10.0-windows`, **x64 only**, Windows-only Win32/XInput.
- PoE2 client — **not PoE1**. Do not port PoE1 offsets or assumptions.

## File organization

- Split large types with `partial class` by concern (`RadarApp`, `Poe2Live`) — one file per domain (`RadarApp.WorldReader.cs`, `Poe2Live.MapViewport.cs`).
- Persisted user data under `config/` next to the exe; built-in assets materialized on first run (`icons/`).
